                        URL + a clipboard Copy button (Label not GtkEntry -- a
                        single-line entry hides the dynamic tail behind
                        the identical "https://meshtastic.org/e/#" prefix
                        and the user cannot tell when the URL changed). URL
                        builder lives in libpipnode-core (pn-mesh-qr
                        .{c,h}) as a pure-C, GTK-free port of pip-mesh's
                        build_channel_set_hex + print_qr_url; cairo render (and
                        the libqrencode include) lives in the gui-side
                        page-share.c so the core tier stays headless.

                        ChannelSet wire layout (pip-mesh-compatible):
                          ChannelSet {
                            repeated ChannelSettings settings = 1; // embedded
                            LoRaConfig               lora     = 2; // optional
                          }
                          ChannelSettings { bytes psk = 2; string name = 3; }
                          LoRaConfig (QR subset):
                            bool use_preset = 1; ModemPreset modem = 2;
                            RegionCode region = 7; uint32 hop_limit = 8;
                        URL = "https://meshtastic.org/e/#" + base64url
                        (RFC 4648 with '+'->'-', '/'->'_', trailing '='
                        stripped) of the serialized ChannelSet.

                        Optional dep: libqrencode (PKG_CHECK_MODULES, AC_DEFINE
                        HAVE_QRENCODE, AM_CONDITIONAL); auto-detected, URL-only
                        fallback paints a "install libqrencode and rebuild"
                        notice in the QR slot when missing. Configure prints
                        "libqrencode not found; Meshtastic Share page will show
                        URLs only" in that case.

                        Files shipped: lib/pn-mesh-qr.{c,h} (core),
                        lib/pn-mesh-page-share.{c,h} (gui); deltas in
                        lib/pn-mesh-dialog.c (third expander on Radio tab,
                        set_state on connect/drop, GtkOverlay loading spinner
                        over the notebook -- see UX FOLLOW-UPS below) and
                        lib/Makefile.am (QRENCODE_CFLAGS/LIBS on the gui lib).
                        Unit test tests/unit/ test-pn-mesh-qr.c (5 cases, 19
                        checks) pins byte-for-byte URL match for a single
                        default channel and for the full-config form, plus
                        skip-disabled, selection-subset and empty-error paths.

                        UX FOLLOW-UPS landed with Phase 6:

                        - Handshake loading overlay. The 3-5s handshake would
                        otherwise let the user switch to a tab whose state
                        hasn't arrived and read it as "device has no channels /
                        no MQTT". Notebook is now wrapped in a GtkOverlay with a
                        64x64 centred GtkSpinner + "Reading configuration from
                        device…" label; show_loading/hide_loading also flip
                        notebook sensitivity so tabs cannot be clicked while the
                        spinner is up. drop_connection hides it too so a
                        dialog-close mid-handshake leaves no ghost widget.

                        - Channels page list height. set_min_content_height(220)
                        + set_propagate_natural_height(TRUE) + a hard
                        set_size_request(list, -1, 200) on the GtkListBox
                        itself. Without all three, the FALSE/ FALSE-packed
                        Channels expander pinned the scrolled list to a single
                        row. Same pattern (with smaller numbers) used for the
                        Share page's channel checkbox list -- the QR area's
                        set_size_request was eating the slack the list needed.

                        - Trash-can delete glyph. Per-row delete on the Channels
                        page uses "user-trash-symbolic" (verified present in the
                        icon theme) instead of "edit-delete"; reads as "discard"
                        rather than "erase".

                        GOTCHAS for future cousins (Phase 7 / 11+):

                        (i) ProtoBuf field numbers in pip-mesh's bash docstrings
                        were not always accurate (Phase 5 already hit this on
                        set_channel: docstring 32, code 33). For Phase 6 the
                        field numbers came verbatim out of build_channel_set_hex
                        / print_qr_config and matched what the firmware expects;
                        the test pins them at the URL level so a future "tidy
                        up" cannot silently drift.

                        (ii) Region UNSET would brick the receiver on
                        full-config import (proto3 zero == UNSET, no fall-back).
                        refresh_url skips emission in full-config mode unless
                        PnMeshState->have_lora_config is TRUE (a small dim
                        notice paints in its place) so the URL/QR pair stays
                        blank (not "garbage URL") until the handshake actually
                        surfaces a LoRa config.

                        (iii) Cairo QR render budgets four modules of quiet zone
                        around the matrix even though Meshtastic phone apps are
                        tolerant; without it the white border collapses when the
                        dialog uses a dark theme and decode rate drops. Drawing
                        happens against the cached URL so toggle->draw is one
                        cycle of queue_draw -- no re-encode on every expose.

                        (iv) GtkScrolledWindow's set_min_content_height ALONE
                        was repeatedly observed to be ignored when the scrolled
                        window lives inside a GtkExpander packed FALSE/FALSE in
                        a tab box: the listbox collapsed to one row. The
                        reliable recipe is min_content_height +
                        propagate_natural_height + an explicit
                        gtk_widget_set_size_request on the listbox itself. Any
                        future tab-hosted scrolled list (Phase 7 test page,
                        Phase 11+ module pages) should follow the same
                        belt-and-braces pattern.

                        (v) Long URLs in a single-line GtkEntry hide their
                        dynamic suffix behind the (identical) URL prefix.
                        Wrapping selectable GtkLabel was the right widget; reuse
                        it for any other "show me this URL" affordance instead
                        of an entry.
