[ ] 46 Tasmota Devices dialog. A "Tasmota Devices" entry in the editor's Devices
       menu, modelled on the proprietary zigbee plugin's "Zigbee Devices"
       dialog: pick an MQTT broker profile, and a hidden MQTT session discovers
       and lists every Tasmota device in the left sidebar. Unlike Zigbee (which
       gets a retained bridge/devices inventory all at once), Tasmota discovery
       is poll-based and slow -- each device is asked `cmnd/<dev>/Status 0` and
       answers in its own time -- so the list fills PROGRESSIVELY via the
       incremental row API (pn_device_dialog_add/update_device_row), not a
       one-shot set_device_rows. The discovery mirrors the PnTasmotaProbe +
       PnTasmotaConcentrator worksheet nodes (poll-on-sight, top-level STATUS
       merge), done inline in the dialog over the shared GTK-free parser
       pn-tasmota-common.c (compiled into both the logic and the new -gui
       companion).

         [x] 46.1 Split plugins/tasmota into two tiers (logic pipnode_tasmota.so
               + companion pipnode_tasmota-gui.so), following plugins/shell.
         [x] 46.2 pn-tasmota-gui.c: provider registration, dialog shell, broker
               combo from PnVault, hidden MQTT source/sink, progressive
               discovery list, read-only device-info pane.
         [x] 46.3 Manual GUI verification against a live broker with real
               devices (the list filling in progressively is the acceptance
               criterion). Verified: 10 devices discovered, rows trickling
               "Querying…" -> IP·fw.
         [ ] 46.4 Possible follow-ups (deferred): relay on/off control and
               FriendlyName/config write-back in the info pane; a dedicated menu
               icon instead of the themed "network-wireless".

